.TH DAQ-CLUSTER-CP 1 "2026-09-10" "mu2edaq-shifter-tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
daq-cluster-cp \- copy files to many DAQ cluster nodes in parallel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B daq-cluster-cp
[\fB\-d\fR]
[\fB\-t\fR]
[\fB\-C\fR]
[\fB\-c\fR]
[\fB\-a\fR]
[\fB\-u\fR \fIuser\fR]
[\fB\-j\fR \fIjobs\fR]
[\fB\-v\fR]
[\fB\-n\fR]
\fIfile\fR...
\fIdestination\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B daq-cluster-cp
copies one or more files to the same destination path on every selected
node of the DAQ cluster, running the copies in parallel over a thread
pool.
.PP
All of the files go in a single \fBscp\fR invocation per host, so there
is one ssh handshake per host rather than one per file.
.PP
The node inventory is read from \fIdata/daq_nodes.json\fR, which groups
hosts by subsystem. A host appearing in more than one group is copied
to once; the host order follows the group order
\fBdaq\fR, \fBtrk\fR, \fBcrv\fR, \fBcalo\fR so that output is stable
between runs.
.PP
Selecting no group is the same as \fB\-\-all\fR.
.PP
Every source file is checked for existence before any connection is
made, so a typo fails immediately rather than after a hundred scp
failures.
.SH OPTIONS
Configuration precedence is command line, then environment variable,
then .env file, then built-in default.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-daq
Copy to the \fBdaq\fR nodes.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-trk
Copy to the tracker nodes.
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-crv
Copy to the CRV nodes.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-calo
Copy to the calorimeter nodes.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all
Copy to every node in the inventory.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-user " " \fIUSER\fR
SSH username. Environment: \fBMU2EDAQ_CLUSTER_USER\fR. Default: the
local \fB$USER\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-nodes\-file " " \fIFILE\fR
Alternative node inventory. Default: \fIdaq_nodes.json\fR from the data
directory.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-jobs " " \fIN\fR
Number of copies to run at once. Environment:
\fBMU2EDAQ_CLUSTER_JOBS\fR. Default: \fI16\fR.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
List the selected hosts and report each successful copy, not only the
failures.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Print the scp command lines and copy nothing.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the package version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage summary and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I data/daq_nodes.json
Node inventory, an object mapping group name to a list of hostnames.
Located through \fBMU2EDAQ_DATA_DIR\fR or the installation root.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every host succeeded, or the dry run completed.
.TP
.B 1
At least one host failed, no hosts were selected, or the inventory
could not be read. A per-host failure count is printed on stderr.
.TP
.B 2
A named source file does not exist.
.SH NOTES
\fBscp\fR runs with \fB\-B\fR (batch mode), so it never prompts. Make
sure Kerberos or agent authentication is working first, or every host
will fail at once.
.SH EXAMPLES
Push a configuration file to the tracker nodes:
.PP
.RS
.nf
daq-cluster-cp -t -u mu2edaq tracker.fcl /home/mu2edaq/config/
.fi
.RE
.PP
Check what would happen first:
.PP
.RS
.nf
daq-cluster-cp -n -a tracker.fcl /home/mu2edaq/config/
.fi
.RE
.PP
Push several files everywhere, eight at a time, reporting each:
.PP
.RS
.nf
daq-cluster-cp -a -j 8 -v a.fcl b.fcl /home/mu2edaq/config/
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR daq-network-verify.sh (1),
.BR daq-ls2json (1),
.BR scp (1)
